# KNOWN GAP (filed 2026-08-15 from the R42 Track-D brief-review pass 9,
# orchestrator-verified): the DOCUMENTED postcondition form comparing two
# fields of a tuple return value — `assert return.0 <= return.1`
# (docs/language-design.md + docs/language-reference.md both show it) —
# does NOT parse: only the LEADING `return` is substituted by the parser's
# postcondition rewrite; the second occurrence errs "expected identifier,
# found integer" at `return.1`. Docs-vs-parser divergence (Core #8: the
# documented form is the intended one).
# INTENDED: the form parses, checks, and enforces the postcondition.
# Wired test: assert_return_second_field_parses (tests/integration.rs, #[ignore]d).
(int, int) two():
    assert return.0 <= return.1
    return (1, 2)

void main():
    print(two().0)
